@startuml sequence-import-and-render
!include style.iuml
title Import a BPMN model into a choreography type and render it back (deploy:asset, render:asset)

actor "Authority" as Authority
participant "deploy-local.js" as Deploy
participant "bpmn-builder-js\nimporter" as Importer
participant "choreography-model.js" as ModelCodec
participant "Model contract\n(SSTORE2)" as Model
participant "ChoreographyMutableAsset" as Asset
participant "ChoreographyNMT" as NMT
participant "ChoreographyTokenURIRenderer" as Renderer
participant "web3.js\n(readChoreography)" as Web3
participant "bpmn-builder-js\npipeline" as Pipeline

== Import ==
Authority -> Deploy : deploy:asset paper-example.bpmn
Deploy -> Importer : BPMN XML to NMT dataset (roles, nodes by name)
Importer --> Deploy : dataset
Deploy -> ModelCodec : modelFromDataset, encodeModel
ModelCodec --> Deploy : creation code
Deploy -> Model ** : create
note right of Deploy : then the NMT and a mint,\nas in sequence-deploy-and-mint

== Render ==
Authority -> Web3 : render:asset <asset>
Web3 -> Asset : tokenURI()  (one eth_call)
Asset -> NMT : tokenURI(tokenId)
NMT -> Renderer : tokenURI(asset)
Renderer -> Asset : getRoleNames, getRole,\ngetNodeNames, getNode
Renderer --> Web3 : data:application/json;base64,...
Web3 -> Web3 : decodeTokenURI, buildRawOutput
Web3 -> Pipeline : raw JSON
Pipeline -> Pipeline : normalize, validation,\nprocess-mapper, moddle-generator
Pipeline --> Authority : *.generated.bpmn.xml

note over Renderer
  The JSON is computed from the asset on every call and
  never stored: the BPMN XML is a view of the asset, and
  the model contract is read only when an asset is born.
end note
@enduml
